Corium host packaging for Ubuntu Resolute
========================================

The packaging/ubuntu-resolute branch is the source for the Launchpad
recipe targeting ppa:nmccallum/pichi, resolute only. It contains debian/,
the crates pinned by Cargo.lock in vendor/, and Cargo's complete
.cargo/config.toml, including the Carapace and Devmap Git source redirects.
LICENSE.dependencies records the bundled crates' licenses and notices.

This branch uses source format 3.0 (native), with version 0.2.0. All sources
are in one tree. Launchpad does not need a separate orig tarball or a run
of debian/make-orig-source.py. Build the recipe from this branch.

After installing Build-Depends, source and binary builds need no network
or warm Cargo cache. From a checkout of this branch, run:

    dpkg-buildpackage -S -us -uc
    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

For a clean Resolute build with a locally configured sbuild chroot:

    sbuild --dist=resolute ../corium_0.2.0.dsc

debian/rules gives Cargo a private home and always builds with:

    cargo build --offline --locked --release --bin corium

Its clean target preserves vendor/, including Cargo.toml.orig files covered
by Cargo's checksums. It installs the native host binary to /usr/bin/corium.
Builds are intended for native amd64 and arm64 builders. Package tests are
disabled: the VM tests need QEMU and the non-PID-1 test refuses root.
Upstream's validation requirements still apply before merge.

To refresh dependencies, use a networked machine with Cargo/Rust >= 1.89.
Update Cargo.lock deliberately, then run:

    cargo --config net.offline=false vendor --locked --versioned-dirs vendor

Save the generated source configuration in .cargo/config.toml, including
all Git source redirects, and add one [net] section with offline = true.
Refresh LICENSE.dependencies from the bundled crates' manifests, license
files and notices. Commit vendor/, Cargo.lock, the configuration and notices
together. Review upstream changes before updating this packaging branch.

GitHub main keeps the separate 3.0 (quilt) packaging path. Only on main,
debian/make-orig-source.py prepares an orig tarball for local quilt builds;
see main's debian/README.source for those instructions. The recipe on this
branch does not use that helper. Archive setup is handled by Infra.
